  "body": "Part of #1152 (and #290, D7). Found while working #1152.\n\n**What is missing:** the body electrode of #1152 is a prism: one outline extruded along Z. The outline atom (`stock_sim::simulate_outline`) burns only that. So `electrode_from_faces` still refuses, by name:\n\n- a cavity with a drafted (leaning) wall (\"leans N degrees off vertical - a drafted wall or a tilted floor is not modelled\"),\n- a cavity with more than one floor level (\"a stepped cavity, which is not modelled\").\n\n**What is wanted:**\n1. A tool record for an electrode whose section changes with height (a stack of outlines with their Z, or a height for each outline edge).\n2. A sim atom that burns that body through the column grid. It must be exact at each column centre where it can be. Where it cannot, it must not report less removal than the electrode makes.\n3. `sinker_cavity::cavity_of` and the electrode derivation for these two cavity kinds.\n\n**Evidence:** `crates/motion/src/sinker_cavity.rs` (the two refusals), `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/dexel_outline.rs`, `docs/decisions/1152-electrode-body.md`.\n\n**Done means:** the faces of a pocket with drafted walls, and of a pocket with a stepped floor, each yield an electrode whose burn the program verdict (`simulate_document`) judges clean. The same electrode in a smaller cavity is convicted as a gouge. Synthetic conditions only; state \"not exercised on a real EDM control\".\n\nLabels wanted (this account cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `P4`, `effort:max`, `area:sim`, `source:agent`.\n",
